    {
      "id": "233e3db6-3e50-4d01-9b2f-db44912d870a",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1376,
        -96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Automated AI based news editor\n### How it works\n\n1. Triggers manually and sets workflow configuration variables like Telegram chat ID.\n2. Fetches headlines from various RSS feeds (World, Tech, Business, Markets, Science) and merges them into a single list.\n3. Filters the combined list to remove duplicates, sorts them by newest first, and limits the output to 70 headlines.\n4. Aggregates the filtered headlines and constructs a prompt for the AI model.\n5. Uses Google Gemini to select the most relevant news and summarize them into a daily digest.\n6. Logs the generated digest to Google Sheets and sends it as a message to Telegram.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- - [ ] Connect your Google Gemini API credentials.\n- - [ ] Connect your Google Sheets account and configure the target spreadsheet.\n- - [ ] Connect your Telegram Bot credentials and update the Chat ID in the CONFIG node.\n- - [ ] Update the RSS feed URLs if you wish to follow different topics or sources.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the number of limited headlines and modify the Gemini prompt to change the style and tone of the generated digest."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
